.page expand 1 convert tabs to spaces

# SYNOPSIS
*expand* [*-t* _N_] [_FILE_]

# DESCRIPTION
`expand` copies _FILE_ (or standard input) to standard output with every tab character replaced by enough spaces to reach the next tab stop. Tab stops are every 8 columns unless `-t` is given. Only one file is read.

# OPTIONS
@ *-t* _N_
    Put the tab stops _N_ columns apart.

# EXAMPLES
    expand -t 4 Makefile | less
    expand source.c > spaces.c

# SEE ALSO
pnote(1), fold(1), tr(1)
